# JS/TS files are formatted by ESLint (@stylistic) — not Prettier.
# Prettier handles JSON, YAML, CSS, and Markdown only.
# (All JS/TS/JSX/TSX variants are listed so the per-package `prettier --write .`
#  — which scopes via this ignore file, not an extension glob — stays off them.)
*.cjs
*.cts
*.js
*.jsx
*.mjs
*.mts
*.ts
*.tsx

# Component SFCs, for exactly the same reason — Prettier claims `.vue` out of the box. The
# two genuinely disagree: Prettier writes `{ required: [...values] }` where
# `@stylistic/object-curly-spacing` (as configured here) wants `{ required: [...values]}`, so
# `pnpm prettier:fix` and `pnpm lint` would undo each other forever on any Vue file.
# `.svelte` is listed pre-emptively: Prettier claims it only once `prettier-plugin-svelte` is
# installed, which is a dependency away from the same conflict.
*.svelte
*.vue

# Lockfiles — managed by package manager, never reformat
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# The workspace manifest — hand-authored, and Prettier fights the author over it.
#
# Prettier rewrites single-quoted YAML scalars to double quotes, so every `overrides:` entry would
# churn the moment anyone touches this file for an unrelated reason: a few lines of comment would
# arrive as a whole-block diff in the file that carries the repo's supply-chain policy, and reviewing
# a policy change would mean reading past a screen of quote flips.
#
# Single and double quotes are equivalent in YAML for every value here (no escapes, no leading
# sigils), so there is nothing to gain and a reviewable diff to lose. The quoting also matters to
# `tests/tooling/overrideUpperBounds.test.ts`, which reads the single-quoted override ranges.
pnpm-workspace.yaml

# The local pnpm content-addressable store.
#
# 🔴 `pnpm prettier:check` globs `**/*.{...,json,...}`, and the store holds ~900 package manifests.
# Without this entry the check reports hundreds of files nobody owns, and real drift in tracked
# sources disappears into that noise. A gate whose output cannot be read is not a gate.
.pnpm-store/

# Transient run artifacts.
tmp/
test-results/

# Build output (generated — never format)
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/

# Mock data
packages/mock-data/src/**/*.json
packages/mock-data/dist/**/*.json

# Verbatim license texts — legal instruments that must match their canonical upstream form
# byte for byte. Never reformat these.
#
# 🔴 `LICENSE.md` is the verbatim Apache-2.0 text. Prettier would reflow it on the next commit that
# touched it, silently, so it must stay listed here (`tests/tooling/licenseDeclarations.test.ts`
# asserts that it is, alongside the matching `.markdownlint-cli2.yaml` ignore).
LICENSE.md

# Notice copies generated into each package by `scripts/sync-licenses.mjs` (gitignored). The sync strips
# relative links, which rewraps lines, so they are not Prettier-formatted output. (The license copies are
# already covered by the `LICENSE.md` entry above, which matches at any depth.)
packages/*/NOTICE.md
